#   "MUST NOT RELINK" is the one rule here with teeth, and it is the reason a   #
#   Makefile is asked for at all: running `make` twice with nothing changed in  #
#   between must do nothing the second time. That is a statement about          #
#   PREREQUISITES -- what each target is declared to depend on -- not about     #
#   the commands in the recipes.                                                #
#                                                                              #
#   SRC is left empty deliberately. "Files to submit: Makefile and all the      #
#   necessary files" fixes no source filenames, so how you split the program    #
#   is yours to decide, not this stub's.                                        #
